@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"
@type = "koroneiki"

Feature: Koroneiki Account and Contact Role API
	Testing Koroneiki Account API functionality in relation to Contact Roles.

Teardown:
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following names
	| Koroneiki Auto Subsidiary |
	| Koroneiki Engr Subsidiary |
	| Koroneiki Automotive      |
	| Koroneiki Engineering     |
	* I tear down the contacts on koroneiki with the following email addresses
	| koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| koroneiki.contact2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I tear down the contact roles on koroneiki with the following names
	| Default Team Role  |
	| Optional Team Role |
	* I tear down the teams on koroneiki with the following names
	| Development Team |
	| Marketing Team   |
	| Engineering Team |
	| Sales Team       |

Scenario: Assign team contact role to contact
	Koroneiki contacts should be able to be assigned to team contact roles on teams.

	Given I create a contact on koroneiki with the following values
	| Email Address | koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | Koroneiki                                |
	| Language      | English                                  |
	| Last Name     | Contact1                                 |
	| Middle Name   | User                                     |
	And I create a contact role on koroneiki with the following values
	| Description | This is the default role for teams |
	| Name        | Default Team Role                  |
	| Type        | Team                               |
	And I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code         | KORAUTO                                  | |
	| Description  | Test automotive account on koroneiki     | |
	| Fax Number   | 555-555-1234                             | |
	| Name         | Koroneiki Automotive                     | |
	| Phone Number | 555-555-5678                             | |
	| Region       | United States                            | |
	| Status       | Active                                   | |
	| Tier         | T4                                       | |
	| Website      | www.koroneikiautomotive.com              | |
	And I create a team with the name "Development Team" for the account "Koroneiki Automotive"
	And I assign contacts with the following email addresses to the team "Development Team"
	| koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	And I assign the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" on the team "Development Team" to the following roles	
	| Default Team Role |
	Then the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" assigned the team "Development Team" should have the contact role "Default Team Role"
	And the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" assigned the team "Development Team" should have the contact role "Member"

Scenario: Assign team contact role to contact via uuid
	Koroneiki contacts should be able to be assigned to team contact roles on teams via uuid.

	Given I create a contact on koroneiki with the following values
	| Email Address | koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | Koroneiki                                |
	| Language      | English                                  |
	| Last Name     | Contact1                                 |
	| Middle Name   | User                                     |
	And I create a contact role on koroneiki with the following values
	| Description | This is the default role for teams |
	| Name        | Default Team Role                  |
	| Type        | Team                               |
	And I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code         | KORAUTO                                  | |
	| Description  | Test automotive account on koroneiki     | |
	| Fax Number   | 555-555-1234                             | |
	| Name         | Koroneiki Automotive                     | |
	| Phone Number | 555-555-5678                             | |
	| Region       | United States                            | |
	| Status       | Active                                   | |
	| Tier         | T4                                       | |
	| Website      | www.koroneikiautomotive.com              | |
	And I create a team with the name "Development Team" for the account "Koroneiki Automotive"
	And I assign contacts with the following email addresses to the team "Development Team" via uuid
	| koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	And I assign the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" on the team "Development Team" to the following roles via uuid	
	| Default Team Role |
	Then the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" assigned the team "Development Team" should have the contact role "Default Team Role" visible via uuid
	And the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" assigned the team "Development Team" should have the contact role "Member" visible via uuid

Scenario: Assign separate team contact roles to contacts
	Separate koroneiki team contact roles should be able to be assigned to separate contacts on a team.

	Given I create a contact on koroneiki with the following values
	| Email Address | koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | Koroneiki                                |
	| Language      | English                                  |
	| Last Name     | Contact1                                 |
	| Middle Name   | User                                     |
	And I create a contact on koroneiki with the following values
	| Email Address | koroneiki.contact2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | Koroneiki                                |
	| Language      | English                                  |
	| Last Name     | Contact2                                 |
	| Middle Name   | User                                     |
	And I create a contact role on koroneiki with the following values
	| Description | This is the default role for teams |
	| Name        | Default Team Role                  |
	| Type        | Team                               |
	And I create a contact role on koroneiki with the following values
	| Description | This is the optional role for teams |
	| Name        | Optional Team Role                  |
	| Type        | Team                                |
	And I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code         | KORAUTO                                  | |
	| Description  | Test automotive account on koroneiki     | |
	| Fax Number   | 555-555-1234                             | |
	| Name         | Koroneiki Automotive                     | |
	| Phone Number | 555-555-5678                             | |
	| Region       | United States                            | |
	| Status       | Active                                   | |
	| Tier         | T4                                       | |
	| Website      | www.koroneikiautomotive.com              | |
	And I create a team with the name "Development Team" for the account "Koroneiki Automotive"
	And I assign contacts with the following email addresses to the team "Development Team"
	| koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| koroneiki.contact2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	And I assign the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" on the team "Development Team" to the following roles	
	| Default Team Role |
	And I assign the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact2@lrcustomer.com.broken" on the team "Development Team" to the following roles	
	| Optional Team Role |
	Then the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" assigned the team "Development Team" should have the contact role "Default Team Role"
	And the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" assigned the team "Development Team" should have the contact role "Member"
	And the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact2@lrcustomer.com.broken" assigned the team "Development Team" should have the contact role "Optional Team Role"
	And the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact2@lrcustomer.com.broken" assigned the team "Development Team" should have the contact role "Member"
	And the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" assigned the team "Development Team" should not have the contact role "Optional Team Role"
	And the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact2@lrcustomer.com.broken" assigned the team "Development Team" should not have the contact role "Default Team Role"

Scenario: Assign team contact roles to contact
	Multiple koroneiki team contact roles should be able to be assigned to a single contact on a team.

